# promise: #709
# Arc's ⌘E ("Open pinned extensions picker."): held ⌘ and E opens the Site Control Center with its first extension
# ringed, each E after it rings the next (round to the first again past the last), and letting go of ⌘ closes it
# and opens the ringed extension's popup, as a click on its tile does. Cra's ⌘E only opened the Site Control
# Center. The keys go through the app's event queue as typed ones do; from the command bar (no ⌘ held) it opens
# as the sliders button does, nothing ringed. The decision is ExtensionPickerTests.
budget rss=900 stalls50=30
pace 0.5
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/Extension
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/SidePanelExtension
relaunch
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=picker
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1

# ⌘E: the first extension (by name: no pins) is ringed.
cra://debug?key=e,14,1048576
wait 1
cra://debug?siteControlsRead=first
expect-log site controls picked first: Cra Scenario Fixture$
# E again, ⌘ still held: the next one, then round to the first.
cra://debug?key=e,14,1048576
wait 0.5
cra://debug?siteControlsRead=second
expect-log site controls picked second: Cra Side Panel Fixture$
cra://debug?key=e,14,1048576
wait 0.5
cra://debug?siteControlsRead=round
expect-log site controls picked round: Cra Scenario Fixture$
# ⌘ let go: the Site Control Center closes and the ringed extension's popup opens.
cra://debug?flags=0
expect-log extension picker: runs Cra Scenario Fixture$
expect-log extension popup shown
wait 1
cra://debug?siteControlsRead=after
expect-log site controls: closed
cra://dismiss
wait 1

# From the command bar's row (no ⌘ held): the Site Control Center as its button opens it, nothing ringed.
cra://action/openExtensions
wait 1
cra://debug?siteControlsRead=bar
expect-log site controls picked bar: none$
# Letting go of ⌘ then runs nothing: it stays up.
cra://debug?flags=0
wait 1
cra://debug?siteControlsRead=still
expect-log site controls picked still: none$
